# One URL per document. The sitemap, the canonical tags and the internal links
# all use the extensionless, no-trailing-slash form, so anything else has to be
# a redirect rather than a second address that answers 200.
#
# The trailing-slash form served the page outright before this file existed, and
# it also broke the relative asset paths in the markup (`/about/` resolves
# `assets/cc-white.png` to `/about/assets/cc-white.png`), so this fixes a real
# rendering bug as well as the duplicate URL.
#
# One placeholder rule covers the whole flat site; there is nothing to add here
# when a page is added. Cloudflare Pages redirects `/about.html` to `/about`
# on its own, so the legacy `.html` entry points keep working without a rule.
#
# /reading-guide is the stable hub for "the book we are reading now." It 308s
# to the current public guide. Swap the destination when the cycle changes;
# archived guides keep their own /guide-<slug> URL.
/reading-guide/  /guide-killing-kryptonite  308
/reading-guide   /guide-killing-kryptonite  308
/blog-post   /blog/the-long-walk  301
/blog-post/  /blog/the-long-walk  301

